  "id": "voluntary-dehydration",
  "term": "voluntary dehydration",
  "definition": "Voluntary dehydration means a person becomes low in body water simply by not drinking enough, rather than through causes such as exercise, heat stress, or diuretics. In this context, it is used as a naturalistic model for studying how insufficient fluid intake may affect cognition and mood.",
